The answer relevancy metric uses LLM-as-a-judge to measure the quality of your RAG pipeline's generator by evaluating how relevant the  of your LLM application is compared to the provided input. deepeval's answer relevancy metric is a self-explaining LLM-Eval, meaning it outputs a reason for its metric score.
:::tip
Here is a detailed guide on RAG evaluation, which we highly recommend as it explains everything about deepeval's RAG metrics.
:::
To use the AnswerRelevancyMetric, you'll have to provide the following arguments when creating an LLMTestCase:
- input
Read the How Is It Calculated section below to learn how test case parameters are used for metric calculation.
The AnswerRelevancyMetric can be used for end-to-end evaluation of text-based and multimodal test cases:
<Tabs items={["Text Based", "Multimodal"]}>
from deepeval.metrics import AnswerRelevancyMetric
from deepeval.test_case import LLMTestCase
from deepeval import evaluate
metric = AnswerRelevancyMetric(
    threshold=0.7,
    model="gpt-4.1",
    include_reason=True
)
test_case = LLMTestCase(
    input="What if these shoes don't fit?",
    # Replace this with the output from your LLM app
    actual_output="We offer a 30-day full refund at no extra cost."
)
# To run metric as a standalone
# metric.measure(test_case)
# print(metric.score, metric.reason)
evaluate(test_cases=[test_case], metrics=[metric])import { AnswerRelevancyMetric } from "deepeval/metrics";
