- [Optional] threshold: a number representing the minimum passing threshold. Can also be set to to run the metric in score-only mode. Defaulted to0.5.
- [Optional] model: a string specifying which of OpenAI's GPT models to use, OR any custom LLM model of typeDeepEvalBaseLLM. Defaulted to .
- [Optional] : a boolean which when set to , will include a reason for its evaluation score. Defaulted to .
- [Optional] : a boolean which when set to , enforces a binary metric score: 1 for perfection, 0 otherwise. It also overrides the current threshold and sets it to 1. Defaulted to .
- [Optional] `async_mode`: a boolean which when set to `True`, enables [concurrent execution within the `measure()` method.](/docs/metrics-introduction#measuring-a-metric-in-async) Defaulted to `True`.
- [Optional] : a boolean which when set to , prints the intermediate steps used to calculate said metric to the console, as outlined in the How Is It Calculated section. Defaulted to .
- [Optional] : of type , which allows you to override the default prompts used to compute the AnswerRelevancyMetricscore. Defaulted todeepeval's default prompts.
- [Optional] flaky: a boolean which when set to , marks the metric as flaky. Defaulted to .
